# Darkmown

Markdown pages that compile into fast, mostly-static websites, with tiny reactive islands only where the document asks for them.

<a class="btn primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
<a class="btn" href="/reactive/">Try reactivity</a>
</section>

:note "Two formats, one rule: .md stays plain CommonMark forever, and renaming to .wd is what unlocks directives, includes, loops, and state."

## What to try

:try "Open the docs route, a .wd page full of includes" href="/docs/"
:try "Open a plain .md page and see directives stay inert" href="/markdown/"
:try "Open the reactive page: state, keyed loops, scoped sections" href="/reactive/"
:try "Open the data page: :fetch, forms into state, persistence" href="/data/"
:try "Open a hidden route and confirm it 404s" href="/-draft/"

## Loops that read like prose

`@loop` is the only loop. Point it at a JSON file, an in-scope value, or a `:state` list, and the body repeats once per row. Includes inside the loop inherit the loop value:

```wd
@loop /features.json into card
@include /feature-card.wd
@endloop
```

@loop /features.json into card
@include /feature-card.wd
@endloop

